Two firms sell an identical product. Inverse demand is P = 110 − Q, where Q is total output. Firm L has a constant marginal cost of 11 and firm F has a constant marginal cost of 20; neither has fixed costs. Firm L chooses its quantity first; firm F observes it and then chooses its own quantity to maximize profit. In the subgame-perfect equilibrium, what is firm L's profit? Reply with only the number.